    "q-103278": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103278",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162998/assets/62412006e358dd798b602547e22eb63c9c274b0d740df885e9c69a1af06bcb97.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠COD$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠EOF$\n\nIII. $m∠COD=m∠DOE$",
      "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠EOF$ are marked with $|$,\n\n- $∠BOC$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $||$, and\n\n- $∠COD$ is marked with $|||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠EOF \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠EOF \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the statements listed is true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
