      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162998/assets/6fe8fc042cc8d5645e9cf0df2fd297e018504c4248a45d348e4778a14caea9ca.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠DOE$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠COD$\n\nIII. $m∠BOC=m∠EOF$",
      "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $|$,\n\n- $∠BOC$ and $∠COD$ are marked with $||$, and\n\n- $∠EOF$ is marked with $|||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠DOE \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠COD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠DOE \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠COD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.",
