    "q-27332": {
      "dom_id": "step-q27332",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162998/assets/bdaee2dee98e41505c8a35c617a8f4fc035125ea8d504efecbe58afc9f7fd06c.png)\n\nIn the figure above,  $m∠CBD=3x+{5}^{∘}$ and $m∠ABD=6x-{19}^{∘}.$ If $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, find $m∠ABC.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CBD & =m∠ABD \\\\ 3x+{5}^{∘} & =6x-{19}^{∘} \\\\ 3x+{24}^{∘} & =6x \\\\ {24}^{∘} & =3x \\\\ {8}^{∘} & =x \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, by the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠CBD+m∠ABD \\\\  & =2(m∠CBD) \\\\  & =2(3({8}^{∘})+{5}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={58}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
